# .trivyignore
# Project: go-url-shortener-cicd-aws
# Last reviewed: 2026-06-04 | Go version at review: 1.24.13
#
# All CVEs listed below are in Go stdlib (standard library).
# Go compiles the entire stdlib into the binary at build time, including
# packages the application never uses. Trivy detects these statically
# but cannot determine runtime reachability.
#
# This application exposes three HTTP/1.1 endpoints only:
#   POST /shorten  — accepts a long URL, returns a short code
#   GET  /:code    — looks up the code, redirects to original URL
#   GET  /health   — returns {"status": "healthy"}
#
# It does not use: TLS, HTTP/2, ReverseProxy, HTML templates,
# email parsing, DNS resolution, or any Windows-specific networking.
# All CVEs below are unreachable in this application's runtime context.
#
# Review policy: on every Go version bump, remove entries whose
# fixed version is now below the current Go version in use.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# net/url — incorrect parsing of IPv6 host literals
# App does not parse or construct URLs with IPv6 host literals
CVE-2026-25679

# crypto/x509, crypto/tls — DoS via certificate chain building
# App does not handle TLS directly; TLS termination is at the ALB
CVE-2026-32280

# crypto/x509 — DoS via inefficient certificate chain validation
# Same reason as above — no direct TLS handling in this app
CVE-2026-32281

# crypto/tls — DoS via multiple TLS 1.3 key operations
# App runs HTTP/1.1 only; TLS is handled upstream by the ALB
CVE-2026-32283

# net — DoS via long CNAME DNS response
# App does not perform DNS lookups or resolve external hostnames
CVE-2026-33811

# net/http — DoS via HTTP/2 SETTINGS frame processing
# App is HTTP/1.1 only and does not enable HTTP/2
CVE-2026-33814

# net/mail — DoS via ParseAddress and ParseAddressList
# App does not parse or handle email addresses
CVE-2026-39820

# net/url — incorrect URL handling edge case
# App only receives user-supplied URLs at POST /shorten;
# does not reach the specific code path described in this CVE
CVE-2026-39823

# net/http/httputil — ReverseProxy forwards hidden query parameters
# App does not use ReverseProxy at any point
CVE-2026-39825

# html/template — script tag injection via trusted template author
# App has no HTML templates; all responses are JSON or HTTP redirects
CVE-2026-39826

# net — panic in Dial/LookupPort via NUL byte on Windows
# App is deployed on Linux (Ubuntu 22.04); Windows-only code path
CVE-2026-39836

# net/mail — DoS via consumePhrase during address parsing
# App does not use the net/mail package anywhere
CVE-2026-42499